{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/972641-mage-lukyanenko-s-edition","id":972641,"title":"Mage: Lukyanenko's Edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-19T12:25:43-07:00","id":972641,"title":"Mage: Lukyanenko's Edition","content":"I hope that some of you have watched <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0403358/?ref_=nv_sr_1\" target=\"_blank\">Night Watch</a> and Day Watch based on Sergei Lukyanenko's <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night_Watch_(Lukyanenko_novel)\" target=\"_blank\">book</a>s. If not , I recommend to watch and read whole hexalogy because it's awesome. In short: russian version of Dresden Files.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://www.wheresthatfrom.com/wtf/ArchivedShots/2007/027_4.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> I'm curious if anyone tried to transport this setting to M:tAw. If not I'll try to write down some more thoughts in this thread.<br /> <br /> What needs to be adressed<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Twilight and its layers, on higher levels time flows faster then on lower ones so it puts you in an advantage if you are higher. It makes Time arcanum less usefull</li> <li>Twilight is a living thing and it can guard a promise you made (there are spells that are hardcoded in it, rules). But what obout Fate?</li> <li>I don't want to strip CofD setting to much so I'm thinking about merging God-Machine and Twilight</li> <li>Keep the Watchtowers and Paths as archetypes</li> <li>Using/entering Twilight is an attainmant that everyone gets but I affraid that it would take some power from Death arcanum</li> <li>Rework Paradox as less abyssal and more about poficiency</li> </ol>Later on I will compile everything in a doc but for now it will be scattered all over the thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 09-20-2016, 09:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T12:41:07-07:00","id":972655,"title":"","content":"3 of the 5 Paths can access Twilight natively, just saying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T12:50:40-07:00","id":972661,"title":"","content":"You are right but Spirit and Death allow you to enter Twilight in their respective kinds of ephemera, not to mention that with Mind you only project your consciousness.<br /> <br /> The setting needs some way to physically enter Twilight, and it's layers, without casting spell's. Hence attainments tied to gnosis(?) I think? Power Stat in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T20:22:37-07:00","id":972902,"title":"","content":"Are there irises to the twilight state?<br /> Use the key and walk on through.<br /> Though those would be a bit rooted in place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T20:29:23-07:00","id":972904,"title":"","content":"They don't have to be.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1747_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1747\" data-vbnamecard=\"1747\">Moinen</a> What about tethering it to Mage Sight? Scrutinizing a spot hard enough already screws with the barrier between the Fallen and the Supernal Worlds. So if you make it a different kind of Scrutiny action that instead mucks up the barrier between physical and twilight you'd have that universal access.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T02:46:36-07:00","id":973009,"title":"","content":"\u200b<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11641_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11641\" data-vbnamecard=\"11641\">Yelesom</a> There are places where the barrier is thinner and even kind of Twilight Loci.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> Thats a great idea! It would allow greater deal of interractions. I forgot to mention that the first step in entering Twilight is a Mage Sight (you look through the shadow under your eyelids into the Twilight). There you can see auras, nimbi, spells and true forms of entities e.g. a very old vampire that is beautifull in normal world can look like saggy bat-human in lower layers of Tw.<br /> <br /> The weakest Other's(mages, vampires and werewolves) can anly look into Tw and not for long. As the Other becomes stronger he can cast/throw shadow over self and walk right through it. Into the first layer that is sucking your life energy, making you cold and eventually a lifeless shell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T04:26:28-07:00","id":973033,"title":"","content":"So, the way the Supernal works (with different depths, mages being able to reach peripheral/active/focused and archmages being ale to vanish into the deeper realm) in 2e was partly inspired by the Watch books, which I have a great fondness for and wished more people read.<br /> <br /> Can't remember - did it make it as one if the inspirations in the final book?<br /> <br /> Anyways, putting the ephemeral state of Twilight between peripheral and active would be a good start. You should probably collapse the Underworld, Shadow, and Astral into the Supernal World as well.<br /> <br /> A stripped down Awakening where the Supernal is the only otherworld. Ghosts and Cthonians become Shades, 